<title>GERMANY: Bayer to pay $270 mln to settle haemophiliac suit.</title>
<headline>Bayer to pay $270 mln to settle haemophiliac suit.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Bayer AG said on Wednesday four pharmaceuticals groups will pay $600 million to compensate next of kin of over 6,000 haemophiliacs in the United States who contracted AIDS by using tainted blood products.</p>
<p>Bayer said its portion of the payout would total $270 million.</p>
<p>Bayer, along with Baxter International Inc, Armour Pharmaceuticals, a division of Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc and Alpha Therapeutic Corp, a division of Japan's Green Cross Corp agreed to the deal in principle last year.</p>
<p>But Bayer said the final decision was reached by a U.S. judge on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
